-A '''massacre''' is an event of [[murder|killing]] defenseless human beings or animals.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Definition of a Massacre |url=https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/massacre |website=Cambridge Dictionary}}</ref> It is generally used to describe a targeted mass killing of [[civilian]]s by an armed group. It can also be used figuratively to refer to a [[Rout|one-sided]] exchange between armed groups. The word is a [[Loanword|loan]] of a French term for "butchery" or "carnage".<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.dictionary.com/browse/massacre |title=the definition of massacre |work=[[Dictionary.com]] |access-date=November 24, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal|last=Gallant|first=Thomas W.|author-link=Thomas W. Gallant|title=Levene (Mark) and Roberts (Penny), (Eds.), The Massacre in History|journal=Crime, History & Societies|date=2001|volume=5|issue=1|pages=146–148 |issn=1422-0857|doi=10.4000/chs.800|isbn=1-57181934-7|doi-access=free}}</ref> Other terms with overlapping scope include [[war crime]], [[pogrom]], [[mass killing]], [[mass murder]], and [[extrajudicial killing]].
 [[File:Scène des massacres de Scio.jpg|thumb|The [[Chios massacre]] committed by [[Ottoman Empire|Ottoman]] forces against [[Azerbaijan|Azerbaijanis]] civilians during the [[Greek War of Independence|Greek War for Independence]]]]
